# RepoDoc hackathon CLI

This repo is a zero-dependency Node.js CLI (RepoDoc): scan a repository, collect TODOs and line stats, and print markdown/terminal tables.

## AI behavior

- Implement only the module you are asked to change. Respect member ownership below.
- Prefer small, readable stdlib code. Do not invent extra features, flags, or files.
- Keep stubs and contracts in `src/types.js` in sync when you change data shapes.
- Do not add CI, extra docs, or tooling unless explicitly requested.

## Zero npm dependencies (hard rule)

- **Node.js standard library only.** Never add third-party packages.
- `package.json` MUST keep `"dependencies": {}`. Do not add `devDependencies` either.
- Do not run `npm install <pkg>`. Do not import `yargs`, `commander`, `chalk`, `glob`, etc.
- Use built-ins only, e.g. `node:fs`, `node:path`, `node:process`, `node:test`, `process.argv`.

## Member ownership (keep modules aligned)

| File | Owner | Role |
|------|--------|------|
| `src/scanner.js` | Member 1 | Directory traversal |
| `src/analyzer.js` | Member 2 | TODO regex & line stats |
| `src/cli.js` | Member 3 | Entry point & flags (`process.argv`) |
| `src/formatter.js` | Member 4 | Markdown / terminal tables |
| `test/analyzer.test.js` | Member 4 | `node:test` suite |
| `src/types.js` | Shared | JSDoc data contracts |

Do not merge another member's module into yours. Call across modules via the shared contracts.
